 ## Overview
-Photon Beam Tracing is a volumetric radiance estimation method where photon paths are stored as beam segments rather than points, allowing for density estimation via beam intersection [S1]. It differs from standard volumetric photon tracing by storing the photon energy up to the point of intersection with solid geometry, rather than discarding the photon upon collision [S1]. The photon beams map contains a superset of the information in a standard photon map [S1].
